<title>HONG KONG: Tingyi 1996 net rises 11 percent.</title>
<headline>Tingyi 1996 net rises 11 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (U.S. cents)	  1.93	 vs 2.16 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (U.S. cents)   0.36	 vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 17.55 gain vs 20.24 gain</p>
<p>    Net			   79.25	vs 71.40</p>
<p>    Turnover		    483.21     vs 339.35</p>
<p>    Company name		Tingyi (Cayman Islands) Holding Corp</p>
<p>    Books close		 June 4-11</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  to be announced</p>
<p>NOTE - Tingyi is an instant noodle maker.</p>
<p>Exceptional items represent value-added tax compensation and investment grants received.</p>
<p>Share earnings is based on the weighted average of 4.11 billion shares vs 3.30 billion.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 0.36 U.S. cents vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
